      "content": "galingale, the aromatic root of certain East Indian plants of the genera Alpinia and Kæmpferia, used in medicine and cookery (OED s.v. galingale); the rhizoma of Alpinia Galanga, a plant of Java, constitutes the drug known as Radix Galangae majoris or Greater Galangal (Flückiger 582) | the aromatic root of certain East Indian plants, used in medicine and cookery (OED s.v. galigale) | the aromatic root of certain East Indian plants (used in medicine and cookery) (OED s.v. galingale) | the aromatic root of certain East Indian plants (used in medicine and cookery) (OED s.v. galingale) 48, 158, | the aromatic root of certain East Indian plants, used in medicine and cookery (Heyd 591-3)"
